! Sol-Handwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit) — hands room handback

&lt;&lt;~ stance "philosopher">> &lt;&lt;~ mu "_!">>
->✶ ''MEASURED scope.'' This read used the span-head source and road; it ran no suite and changed no repo file. The road calls the session contract approved in outline while naming twelve build debts [[session-contract.mem:34,291-304|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]. Treat a specified module without a production caller as design evidence, not a closed row.

->⏿ ''What stands.'' The table separates code already serving callers from code awaiting its caller. Lines point into the main checkout.

| Rows | MEASURED standing and gap |h
| F1, F2, P13 | Mesh defines the scoped view, `mountSurface`, and `resolveSurfaceRecipe`; production still calls `mountWiki` and selects plugin CIDs through the narrower resolver. Node and browser compose sites still need session facets, the one effective recipe, per-meme grants, and the leaf gate. The temporary node fleet bridge lets the worn face read vessel books [[road:592-593|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; [[pool:388,445|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts]]; [[fleet-view:19-25|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/face-fleet-view.ts]]; [[browser:428-438|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]]. |
| F3, F4, F5 | Face-secret `(face,wiki,kind)` working addresses lack production binding. UDS already persists request facts and outcomes, yet opens by socket without a verified face; its digest still includes caller `requestedBy`. Node session open, face-bound receipt reads, effect index placement and a durable surface settle receipt remain owed [[contract:98-108,186-206|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]; [[UDS:32,527-530,639-646|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/uds-channel.ts]]; [[road:462-464|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]. |
| F6, B2 | Holder routing, epoch fencing and asker-directed sealing have code; `session:open` still lacks its production face supplier, while the remaining Repo/daemon ownership move and two-tab/two-face proof await closure [[road:594,601|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; [[holder:578-594|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/shared-holder-core.ts]]; [[browser:490-563|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]]. |
| F9, A8, W17 | Wave D retired the persisted active-face selector, while the live `persona wear` switch, its five-phase fence and second joined face on one vessel remain owed [[road:569,586,596|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; [[contract:257-263|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]. |
| F10, F11, F12 | Fleet view and removal lack the person-facing path; a long-silent device must catch up causally. Watch names `--to` without a lease; the seat lacks a standing-grant session and profile parity; parallel drafts trust `modifier` or actor ID rather than the verified change face [[road:465-467|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; [[drafts:211-212|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/parallel-drafts.ts]]; [[contract:79-90,279-280|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]. |
| G13 | Summons consumes by tombstoning every holding bag, while in-memory request tracking and the daemon effect index provide partial replay protection. Writer proof, working-only tombstone, durable lease/fence and audience check remain owed [[road:471|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; [[summons:48-51|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-summons.ts]]; [[dispatcher:273-314,396-409|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-dispatcher.ts]]. |
| I2 | Place the separately scouted far-agent relay after a face intent plane and a standing seat, with agent signature preserved through relay admission. Do not let its relay mint a face act [[face-intent-plane.mem:86-92,147-149|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem]]. |

->◇ ''LEAD — model joints.'' Canon rules: “A session wears the face and the vessel wears none” [[road:107|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]]; “Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session” [[contract:61|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]; “The door carries; the hand authorizes” [[contract:85|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]. Thus F3/4/5/9/11 and A8 share one session/working/receipt/switch model; F1/2/P13 and browser F6/B2 must consume that model together at the surface boundary. F12 attribution and G13 summons consume its signer and working layer, but each can land as a later whole model. F10 can land alone after verified face fleet reads. I2 can land alone after I1 and the seat. House law derives one owner Repo, capability-scoped reads, and no clock-based authority lapse from the approved contract [[contract:114-144,246-249|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]].

One ''operator joint'' remains worth asking before coding: when a face participates in two Nexuses, should one live session name `(face,Nexus)` at open, or should one face session expose both through separately bounded facets? Lean: name the Nexus at open, preserving one proof subject and one recipe per generation; the contract itself flags this gap [[contract:295|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]]. Until that answer, keep a one-Nexus session bound explicit; avoid an implicit current Nexus.

->▶ ''Build order; each slice starts red, carries a control, then proves a known positive.''

# ''K15 bonds first; then session spine'' (F3/4/5/9, A8, W17). K15 already owns the selected face atom and faceless-vessel rule; let it finish signing before session callers encode authority. Shared files: node/browser openers and CLI face choice, especially their identity hunks; session work takes the later open/call hunks. Red: two concurrent node sessions cross-read a receipt or copied socket, old generation signs, or wrong-face working address opens. Control: same-face later CLI reads its receipt; A and B run concurrently. Positive: selected atom signs each face operation, faceless vessel serves floor only. Hold `session-contract`, `session-face/signer`, UDS, verb VM, working-slot resolver, CLI `persona`, node opener. ''Identity and genesis bytes move here through K15 and working-address genesis; finish before bake.'' [[K15 brief|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/brief.md]]; [[contract:190,259-263|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]].
# ''Scoped surfaces and holder'' (F1/2/6, P13, B2). Red: arbitrary foreign document or catalog name leaks, two tabs share an island or reply, stale port paints, browser starts a second Repo. Control: same-face permitted bag and content read, two same-face tabs get distinct islands, failed boot retries. Positive: node and browser each resolve a recipe at mount, one holder owns Repo/daemon, asker seals, leaf sync obeys one-way gate. Hold pool/view/recipe, node/browser compose callers, holder, TW5 view port and kernel. ''Heavy D2 overlap:'' TW5 island/port, hand gate, projection sink, and the opener port-lease hunks; serialize final integration against D2's landed port interface. ''K15 overlap:'' opener face-supplier and sealer hunks; merge after its signer lands. No new identity bytes, but recipe and working binding affect founding shape [[road:592-594|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem]].
# ''Hands and attribution'' (F11 remainder, F12, F10). Red: unleased file edits sign, stale watch generation commits, standing seat signs authority, spoofed `modifier` gains face attribution, silent fleet device acts before catch-up. Control: attended direct ask edits only named tiddlers; standing seat drafts; verified change labels its face; current fleet device acts. Positive: watcher leases a face wiki, MCP and CLI share refusals and receipts, Mask travels as a non-authorizing field. Hold watch/projector, MCP adapter, profile gate, parallel drafts, fleet UI/removal. D2 touches projector/projection sink; take its landed hand gate. K15 touches fleet signer and face removal only at API edges. ''Authorship record format and fleet relation bytes merit pre-bake closure.'' [[contract:71-90|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem]].
# ''Intent and effects'' (G13; I2 after I1). Red: forged writer, duplicate after restart, wrong audience, relay alters argument, revoked agent grant admits. Control: fresh authorized intent executes once, independent audience slots answer, valid far agent reaches a face device. Positive: working-only tombstone, durable lease/fence and effect receipt; relay countersigns admission only. Hold dispatcher/summons, effect reader, intent-plane adapter and relay seat. K15 supplies atom verification; G15's after-roll chain supplies the causal fence; D2 shares no core file. ''Intent log/receipt formats and relay grant bytes move before bake if genesis seeds them'' [[face-intent-plane.mem:45-52,86-92|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem]].

->↺ ''Builder's price.'' Lane 1 shapes every later caller; lane 2 carries the highest merge cost through both vessel openers and D2's island ports; lane 3 follows the mounted surface; lane 4 follows the face signer and working receipt. Ink & Switch's [[local-first account|https://www.inkandswitch.com/essay/local-first/]] supports separate private working versions before promotion; [[Keyhive's capability model|https://www.inkandswitch.com/project/keyhive/]] sharpens the face-grant boundary. Neither source supplies this house's session law; the cited canon does.

